**How to implement.** The start screen's window: it composes the screen's context from the app scope and hands an opened kit to the constructor of its mode, through the import dialog when the kit's snapshot needs a decision (001 §F 'Choosing a kit opens the constructor in that mode'; 001 §O: every new window calls `WindowFit.keepOnScreen` and joins `ScrollExtentTests`; the S5.2 brief: a new window with its own view and window files in OpticalConstructor.Ui). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the start-screen group (step 178): `kitStartWindow` (`"KitStartWindow"`) with a one-line doc. (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitStartWindow.fs` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui`, compiled directly after `AppContext.fs`, the list's last file, because it reads the app scope: one `<Compile>` line and no comment. `type KitStartWindow(context : AppContext, mode : ConstructorMode, pickerFor : TopLevel -> KitFolderPicker, showConstructor : ConstructorMode -> OpenedKit -> unit)` inherits `HostWindow`, as `LibraryWindow` does (`LibraryWindow.fs:LibraryWindow`); its doc is one to three lines citing 001 §F and spec 0050 S5.2. Its title is `Open a kit — Main` for `ForwardConstructor` and `Open a kit — Inverse` for `InverseConstructor`; its `Name` and `AutomationId` are `ConstructorUiId.kitStartWindow`; it asks for 720 × 560 and then calls `WindowFit.keepOnScreen this` (`WindowLayout.fs:WindowFit.keepOnScreen`). It captures the Elmish dispatch from its init command as `LibraryWindow` does, and runs `Program.mkProgram` over `initKitStart`, `updateKitStart` and `kitStartView` (steps 176 to 178) with the context `{ kitHistory = context.kitHistory; limit = context.settings.kitHistoryLimit; clock = ClockProvider.system; author = KitAuthor Environment.UserName; imports = context.catalogueImports; picker = pickerFor this; showKit = <the hand-off> }` (steps 150, 154, 163, 175: the clock, the author and the picker the launcher's open composed). The hand-off of `opened` is `opened.resolveAndShow context.catalogueImports (fun shown -> showConstructor mode shown; this.Close ()) (fun e -> dispatch (KitOpenFailed e))` (step 174): a kit whose snapshot needs a decision opens the import dialog first; a shown kit opens the constructor of the screen's mode and closes the screen; a failed re-binding is shown on the screen; and a cancelled dialog releases the kit and keeps the screen open. Closing the screen opens and closes nothing else. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs` gains `the kit start screen leaves everything reachable`: `assertReachable "KitStart"` (`ScrollExtentTests.fs:assertReachable`) over a `KitStartWindow` whose context is `TestAppScope.freshAppContext (FolderName "ScrollExtentTests")` with `kitHistory` replaced by an in-memory history holding forty entries (every fifth folder missing, every seventh kit starred), so the list is longer than the screen; its picker is `TestAppScope.kitPickerOf` of a fresh folder and `showConstructor` ignores its kit. (4) `KitStartWindowTests` (step 178) gains, over `TestAppScope.freshAppContext (FolderName "KitStartWindowTests")` with `kitHistory` replaced by a fresh in-memory history, a `showConstructor` that records the mode and the kit, and pickers from `TestAppScope.kitPickerOf`; every recorded kit is closed at the fact's end. Without a trait, `the start screen's title names its mode and it carries its stable id`: the window over `ForwardConstructor` is titled `Open a kit — Main` and over `InverseConstructor` `Open a kit — Inverse`, and each carries `kitStartWindow` as its `Name` and `AutomationId`. With trait `ui-smoke`, `acceptance: New kit opens the new kit in the constructor of the screen's mode, bumps the history and closes the screen`: over a fresh folder, pressing `newKitButton` on the Main screen records `ForwardConstructor` with a read-write kit named for the folder, closes the screen, and leaves the history's one entry that folder; the Inverse screen records `InverseConstructor` the same way.

**Acceptance.** After the window lands, `KitStartWindow` MUST compose its context from the app scope, be titled by its mode, fit its screen, and hand an opened kit through `resolveAndShow` to the constructor of its mode, closing itself; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `acceptance: New kit opens the new kit in the constructor of the screen's mode, bumps the history and closes the screen`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the start screen's title names its mode and it carries its stable id` and `the kit start screen leaves everything reachable`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the fourteen s20 invariants MUST pass.
